sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Proposed protected workspace lifecycle
  accDescr: Compute pins a reservation from the selected Sandbox Driver. After the same original acknowledges signed release, Compute compares all four pins and asks the Driver for bearer-authenticated serving status using the retained admitted requirements. Only serving permits activation. The Gateway authenticates the canonical origin with only the pinned provider CA before it sends the HTTP Upgrade request and bearer. A TLS failure sends neither. On the authenticated connection the relay checks the bearer and released original before returning 101 with one generation proof. The Gateway verifies that proof before sending or accepting native frames.
  participant C as Compute
  participant S as Selected Sandbox Driver
  participant G as Agent Gateway
  participant W as Workspace relay
  Note over C,G: Prepare (no workspace traffic)
  C->>S: Read original workspace binding
  S-->>C: Reserved endpoint and generation
  C->>G: Pin origin, CA, root and generation
  Note over C,W: Activate and connect
  C->>S: Recheck original after signed release
  S-->>C: Observed release state and binding, if available
  alt Same original acknowledged and all four pins match
    C->>S: Read bearer-authenticated harnessStatus
    Note over C,S: Driver uses retained admitted requirements
    alt Authenticated serving result
      S-->>C: Serving
      C->>G: Activate
      G->>W: Start TLS for the canonical origin
      Note over G,W: Gateway authenticates TLS with only the pinned provider CA
      alt TLS authenticates the origin
        G->>W: Send HTTP Upgrade request with bearer
        Note right of W: Check bearer and current released original
        W-->>G: Return 101 and one generation proof
        Note over G,W: Gateway checks for one matching generation before any frame either way
      else TLS authentication fails
        Note over G,W: Close without sending Upgrade or bearer
      end
    else Missing or non-serving result
      S-->>C: Unavailable or not serving
      Note over C,G: Keep the new revision unavailable
    end
  else Held, changed or missing owner or pin
    Note over C,G: Keep unavailable without recreating the pin
  end
